<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bacillus subtilis Turing wavenumber at 16 µm (Holocene detail scale) — Code-to-model traceability: 89/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The dispersion, the discrete Laplacian used in the fit, and the pass-2 comments that explain the longer integration and the dropped mode sit next to the code they describe. The Lean file proves the trace sign, the 16-versus-10 identities, and the ratio-9.2 threshold. Those proofs were not run through a Lean binary here." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bacillus subtilis Turing wavenumber at 16 µm (Holocene detail scale) — Model fidelity to source: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "sigma_plus and the Schnakenberg PDE are the Turing dispersion, calibrated to 16.02 µm linearly. Pass 2 integrates until std(u)=0.27, and the radial FFT then peaks at mode 12 (16.00 µm). The animated colony is a separate kinematic reduction that uses that wavelength; it is not the PDE on a disk." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bacillus subtilis Turing wavenumber at 16 µm (Holocene detail scale) — Morphometric validation: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "On modes n=8 through 20, Pearson r is 0.99998 and RMSE is 0.00110 (pass 1 RMSE was 0.108 because mode n=6 was included). The bulk radial wavelength is 16.00 µm against the 16 µm slot target. The specimen ridge count is 43 against model mode 72, foreground fraction 0.169 against a 0.35 placeholder, and coherency 0.522 against 0.5, so the specimen metrics are not self-copies." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
